investors concerned about the escalating  trade war with China are hoping for some  calm on Wall Street today Dow Jones  Industrials plunged more than 600 points  yesterday their worst loss in more than  four months this followed China's  decision to raise tariffs on 60 billion  dollars in US goods after President  Trump increased tariffs on Chinese  products Ben Tracy is sorting it all out  for us at the White House where the  president seems ready for more conflict  Ben good morning good morning so the  president has already sent out several  tweets this morning about China in one  saying that the u.s. is in a better  position now than if he had reached a  trade deal meanwhile China is vowing to  fight this trade war to the finish well  let you know in about three or four  weeks whether or not it was successful  you never really know right but I have a  feeling it's going to be very successful  President Trump seems confident he's  winning the trade war his advice to  American companies worried about higher  prices due to tariffs stop buying  products from China open your division  or open up your product have it made in  this country as opposed to made in China  frustrated at a lack of progress the  president is now taking the first step  toward imposing tariffs on another  approximately 300 billion dollars worth  of Chinese goods  this would make items Americans  regularly buy 25 percent more expensive  with nearly 5,000 products impacted  you'll feel the effects whether you're  shopping at the supermarket or the  hardware store baby products like infant  formula pacifiers and clothing will get  more expensive and so will Apple  products like iPhones and iPads I would  say it's everything but the kitchen sink  but it turns out kitchen sinks are on  this list too American farmers already  reeling from the first round of tariffs  last year will likely be hit hardest a  farmers have been incredible no country  can get in the way of our farmers  President Trump says he plans to bail  out farmers who've lost business because  of the tariffs with about 15 billion  dollars of tariff revenue that's the tax  US companies are paying to import many  Chinese goods this despite the  president's repeated claim that the  Chinese not Americans are paying the  price for the trade war  no one's winning and clearly everybody  is potentially going to lose and  probably lose a lot more than they  realize  president Trump plans to meet with  Chinese President Xi Jingping at the g20  summit in Japan next month you may see  these two leaders try to work out some  sort of ceasefire face-to-face but so  far there has been no announcement of  any new trade talks leading up to that  meeting Gael all right Thank You Ben  reporting from Washington
 

